{
  "dn20:0.1": "Long Discourses 20 ",
  "dn20:0.2": "The Great Congregation ",
  "dn20:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn20:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Sakyans, in the Great Wood near Kapilavatthu, together with a large Saṅgha of five hundred mendicants, all of whom were perfected ones. ",
  "dn20:1.3": "And most of the deities from ten solar systems had gathered to see the Buddha and the Saṅgha of mendicants. ",
  "dn20:2.1": "Then four deities of the pure abodes, aware of what was happening, thought: ",
  "dn20:2.2": "",
  "dn20:2.3": "",
  "dn20:2.4": "“Why don’t we go to the Buddha and each recite a verse in his presence?” ",
  "dn20:3.1": "Then, as easily as a strong person would extend or contract their arm, they vanished from the Pure Abodes and reappeared in front of the Buddha. ",
  "dn20:3.2": "They bowed to the Buddha and stood to one side. ",
  "dn20:3.3": "Standing to one side, one deity spoke this verse in the Buddha’s presence: ",
  "dn20:3.4": "“There’s a great congregation in the woods, ",
  "dn20:3.5": "where heavenly hosts have assembled. ",
  "dn20:3.6": "We’ve come to this righteous congregation ",
  "dn20:3.7": "to see the invincible Saṅgha!” ",
  "dn20:3.8": "Then another deity spoke this verse in the Buddha’s presence: ",
  "dn20:3.9": "“The mendicants there are immersed in samādhi, ",
  "dn20:3.10": "they’ve straightened their own minds. ",
  "dn20:3.11": "Like a charioteer holding the reins, ",
  "dn20:3.12": "the astute ones